    "https://jobs.careerbeacon.com/details/department-of-geodesy-and-geomatics-engineering-tenuretrack-assistant-professor-in-positioning-navigation-and-timing/2223702?utm_source=University+of+New+Brunswick+%28Academic%29&utm_medium=widget&utm_campaign=refer&utm_content=2223702&utm_term=jobtitle": {
      "title": "Department of Geodesy and Geomatics Engineering: Tenure-Track Assistant Professor in Positioning, Navigation, and Timing",
      "description": "Department of Geodesy and Geomatics Engineering: Tenure-Track Assistant Professor in Positioning, Navigation, and Timing at University of New Brunswick (Academic) | Careerbeacon.com University of New Brunswick (Academic) Department of Geodesy and Geomatics Engineering: Tenure-Track Assistant Professor in Positioning, Navigation, and Timing Fredericton, NB Apply Later Apply Now Discover The Opportunity Fredericton, NB Engineering Experienced Full-time Competition Number: 25-35 The Department of Geodesy and Geomatics Engineering at the University of New Brunswick in Fredericton invites applications for a tenure-track position in Geodesy and Geomatics Engineering at the rank of Assistant Professor. The appointment will commence on 1 January 2027. This position is subject to final budgetary approval. The University of New Brunswick respectfully acknowledges that its Fredericton campus sits on unsurrendered and unceded traditional Wolastoqey land. The lands of Wabanaki people were recognized in a series of Peace and Friendship Treaties to establish an ongoing relationship of peace, friendship and mutual respect between equal nations. The river that runs by our university is known as Wolastoq, along which live Wolastoqiyik, \"the people of the beautiful and bountiful river.\" Wolastoq is also known as the St. John River. The minimum qualification for this appointment is a Ph.D. in Geodesy and Geomatics Engineering or a closely related field. Forward-thinking applicants with a substantial research background in the field of positioning, navigation, and timing (PNT) or adjacent fields are sought for this position. The successful candidate should demonstrate excellence in teaching Geodesy or Geomatics subjects at a university level, ideally in the fields of positioning, navigation, geodesy, or adjustment calculus, and will be required to teach courses that may include GGE 4211: Geodesy II, GGE 3122: Advanced Adjustments, GGE 5042/6042: Kinematic Positioning, or similar subjects. They should be comfortable with online education and ideally have experience teaching mixed classes of in-person and remote students. Applicants must be eligible and willing to register as a Professional Engineer in the Province of New Brunswick. This is an opportunity to join a small but powerful department with a strong international reputation in teaching and research, at a time of growth and new opportunities. They will develop an innovative and impactful research program in PNT and related fields (e.g. simultaneous location and mapping), including collaborations within and outside of the university. They will be expected to supervise students; to be active in service roles; to deliver graduate and undergraduate courses, including courses taught in a hybrid form; and to provide leadership in research and teaching at UNB and in professional, national and international communities. Work will be carried out in English. The successful applicant will join the faculty team at UNB Geodesy and Geomatics Engineering and will work in Fredericton, New Brunswick, Canada. The location of work will be: Department of Geodesy and Geomatics Engineering Head Hall, University of New Brunswick P.O. Box 4400, Fredericton, New Brunswick, Canada E3B 5A3 Review of applications will commence on 25 May 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Letters of application must include a cover letter, curriculum vitae, research statement, evidence of teaching effectiveness (i.e. teaching dossier), and three academic letters of reference. Only those candidates short-listed will be contacted for an interview. Applicants should apply using the \"Apply Now\" button above this ad. Questions concerning this position may be directed to Prof. Robert Kingdon, Chair, Department of Geodesy and Geomatics Engineering, University of New Brunswick (robert.kingdon@unb.ca). The salary range and fringe benefits for this position are defined in the Association of University of New Brunswick Teachers (AUNBT) 2025 - 2029 Collective Agreement sections 35 and 36B. Short-listed candidates will be required to provide satisfactory proof of credentials including appropriately certified translations of credentials into English, as applicable. The University of New Brunswick is committed to employment equity and fostering diversity within our community and developing an inclusive workplace that reflects the richness of the broader community that we serve. The University welcomes and encourages applications from all qualified individuals who will help us achieve our goals, including women, visible minorities, Aboriginal persons, persons with disabilities, persons of any sexual orientation, gender identity or gender expression. Preference will be given to Canadian citizens and permanent residents of Canada. Look for yourself Photo Gallery A little bit about us University of New Brunswick (Academic) The University of New Brunswick employs more than 3,200 full- and part-time staff, including faculty, support staff and students. UNB values people and we have proudly been named as one of Canada\\'s Top 100 Employers for 2026 and one of Atlantic Canada\\'s Top Employers for 2026. UNB is situated on the unceded territory of the Wolastoqiyik and Mi\\'kmaq peoples along the banks of the beautiful and bountiful Wolastoq river, a region recognized worldwide for its natural beauty. UNB is a comprehensive university with a long history of excellence in teaching and research. Apply Now View Careers Page Powered by Apply Later Enter your email to receive a reminder to apply for this position at a later date. * Email Apply Later We will send you an email reminder to with a link to this job. Cancel Create Reminder"
    },
    "https://jobs.careerbeacon.com/apply/2223702?utm_source=University+of+New+Brunswick+%28Academic%29&utm_medium=widget&utm_campaign=refer&utm_content=2223702&utm_term=apply": {
      "title": "Department of Geodesy and Geomatics Engineering: Tenure-Track Assistant Professor in Positioning, Navigation, and Timing",
      "description": "Department of Geodesy and Geomatics Engineering: Tenure-Track Assistant Professor in Positioning, Navigation, and Timing | careerbeacon.com Department of Geodesy and Geomatics Engineering: Tenure-Track Assistant Professor in Positioning, Navigation, and Timing University of New Brunswick (Academic) | Fredericton, New Brunswick, Canada View job description Application Questions Review How would you like to start? Select one of our quick apply options. Import Resume Previous Application Apply Manually Loading... Import Options Contact Information * First name * Last name * Email address * Phone number * Location Languages Add the languages you are fluent in. Language Afrikanns Albanian Arabic Armenian Aymara Basque Bengali Bosnian Bulgarian Cambodian Cantonese Catalan Chechen Chinese (Mandarin) Corsican Croation Czech Danish Dutch Dzongkha English Esperanto Estonian Fiji Finnish French Frisian Galician Georgian German Greek Gujarati Hausa Hawaiian Hebrew Hindi Hungarian Icelandic Indonesian Irish Italian Japanese Javanese Korean Kurdish Lao Latin Latvian Lithuanian Luxembourgish Macedonian Malagasy Malay Malayalam Maltese Maori Marathi Mongolian Nepali Norwegian Pashto Persian Polish Portuguese Punjabi Quechua Romanian Russian Samoan Sanskrit Serbian Slovak Slovenian Somali Spanish Swahili Swedish Tagalog Tajik Tamil Tatar Telugu Thai Tibetan Tonga Tswana Turkish Turkmen Ukranian Urdu Uyghur Uzbek Vietnamese Welsh Wolof Xhosa Yiddish Zulu English * Cover Letter Choose an option below. Both choices are valued equally. Write Cover Letter Attach Cover Letter Rich Text Editor, cover_letter Editor toolbars Basic Styles Bold Keyboard shortcut Command+B Italic Keyboard shortcut Command+I Paragraph Insert/Remove Numbered List Insert/Remove Bulleted List Decrease Indent Increase Indent Align Left Center Align Right Justify Links Link Keyboard shortcut Command+L Unlink about About CKEditor 4 Cover Letter Options * Resume/CV Attach Resume/CV Attachments (Optional) Attach documents that support your application (i.e., transcript or portfolio work) Upload Document Save and Continue Assistant Welcome to your job application! Remember always to put your best foot forward. Be as thorough as possible in the information you provide. Need clarification on something? Just check out the tips I offer you along the way. Tips Contact Information Education Work Experience Languages Core Skills Additional Skills Online Presence Highlights Cover Letter Resume/CV Contact Information I admit this is pretty self-explanatory. But, I do want to remind you to double check your phone number and email address. A tiny mistake could have big implications! Return to tips Education This is where you add all relevant education experience you wish to share. In the description, be sure to add what courses you excelled in and what projects you completed which were really cool. Return to tips Work Experience It’s necessary to share work experience related to the job you are applying for. In the description, be sure to highlight what your major accomplishments were in each previous role. This gives the employer insight into what your responsibilities were and what you are capable of. Use this section to detail any relevant volunteer experience as well. Return to tips Languages Pretty simple. Just select the languages in which you have a working proficiency. Easy peasy. Return to tips Core Skills Mindfully select the skills that help you perform at your best. Core skills are a way for employers to understand you so they can make informed decisions. So be honest ;) Return to tips Additional Skills Have more skills to share? Do it here! Return to tips Online Presence Perhaps you have a stellar blog or a great LinkedIn profile. Share the links here for the employer to explore. Return to tips Highlights The Highlights section appears at the very top of your application. It’s pretty important, so make it count! Highlight key achievements, mention things that stand out about you as a person and your experiences, and if you can, give them a bit of insight into your personality. Help them remember you. You’re amazing, so tell them. Return to tips Cover Letter If you choose Write Cover Letter, you can write it right here in the application. Or you can attach your cover letter (PDF recommended). Return to tips Resume/CV Here you can attach your resume. Attaching your resume here will not overwrite any other info you’ve already imported. We recommend you upload your resume as a PDF file. File types: .pdf,.docx,.doc,.rtf,.txt,.odt Maximum file size is 20 MB. Return to tips Attachments Some employers want to see more. Be sure to check the application to see if they request any additional documentation. Maximum file size is 20 MB. Return to tips Sorry, but it looks like you've missed something. Return to tips Need more help? Uploading file, please wait... Cancel upload × Error: The resume uploaded couldn't be imported properly. Our system only accepts certain file types (.doc, .docx, .pdf for example). If you can convert your file to one of these file types, we should be able to import all of your information. If you experience any issues, you can email us at support@careerbeacon.com . Close Window Log in to your Alongside Account Wrong Username/Email and password combination. Sorry, but it looks like you've already applied for this position. Email address (success) Password (success) Login Forgot Password? SOCIAL LOGIN Login with Facebook Login with LinkedIn Login with Google Close Which profile would you like to use? Sorry, but it looks like you've already applied for this position. Default \n                                  | Last applied position: None Default \n                                  | Last applied position: None"
    },
