in the past, have been disadvantaged in employment. These groups are: women Indigenous people persons with disabilities members of visible minorities UNB is taking special measures to increase the representation of these groups where there are inequities in its workforce. One of the ways we are monitoring the success of these measures is by collecting relevant data. Employment equity policy View UNB's employment equity policy (PDF) AUNBT - UNB joint employment equity committee The members of the committee are: Petra Hauf (Co-Chair) Vice-President (Saint John) UNB Saint John p.hauf@unb.ca Tel: (506) 648-5695 Shawn Quinlan Associate Vice-President People & Culture, UNB Fredericton shawn.quinlan@unb.ca Tel: (506) 458-7676 Lorna Butler Dean, Nursing Faculty of Nursing, UNB Fredericton lorna.butler@unb.ca Tel: (506) 458-7625 Resources About UNB Campus Maps Campus Security Careers at UNB Services at UNB Conference Services Libraries Online & Continuing Ed Leadership Connect with UNB Contact UNB Connect with UNB Contact UNB Resources Toggle navigation About UNB Campus Maps Campus Security Careers at UNB Services at UNB Conference Services Libraries Online & Continuing Ed Leadership © University of New Brunswick Privacy Accessibility Web feedback Close suggested results"
